#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
"""ade-sched: install a checked-in launchd plist on this machine's scheduler (launchd, systemd user units or cron).

usage:
  ade-sched [options] backend               the backend auto-detection picks, its unit/agent dir, the linger state
  ade-sched [options] render PLIST          print what install would write (one `# <path>` header per artifact)
  ade-sched [options] install PLIST         write and activate the job
  ade-sched [options] uninstall LABEL       remove it (not installed: exit 0)
  ade-sched [options] status [LABEL...]     installed / active / next run; no LABEL: every job ade-sched generated
  ade-sched [options] list                  print install.jobs / install.retired_jobs from the install catalog
  ade-sched [options] diff                  compare the catalog to live launchd/systemd/cron/paseo (report only)
  ade-sched [options] reconcile             ADE-owned launchd/systemd/cron/paseo reconcile + ownership ledger (S4b; default dry-run)

options (before or after the subcommand):
  --backend auto|launchd|systemd|cron   default auto (env ADE_SCHED_BACKEND; `none` there turns scheduling off, exit 69)
  --ade DIR             the checkout that fills __ADE__ / @ADE@ (default: the one this script is in; install refuses
                        that default with exit 2 when it is a linked git worktree, which is deleted after its merge)
  --root DIR            catalog root for list/diff/reconcile (default: checkout containing this script)
  --set KEY=VALUE       fill a placeholder, literally as written in the plist (__STATE__=..., @TARGET@=...); repeatable
  --dry-run             install/uninstall: print the artifacts and commands, change nothing;
                        reconcile: plan only (default for reconcile when --yes is absent)
  --yes                 reconcile: execute only admitted writes and write jobs.json; today that is launchd only (an absent-job create+bootstrap, or a bootstrap of an unloaded plist that byte-matches the render); a LOADED job is reloaded or removed only when its installed plist routes through bin/ade-job-run and is provably ADE's (W21c; a run in flight defers it); other loaded jobs, other files, removals that are not so, systemd/cron and paseo steps defer (exit 6)
  --name NAME           reconcile: limit to these logical job names (repeatable)
  --no-activate         install/uninstall/reconcile: write or remove the files, print the activation commands instead of running them
  --restart-service     launchd install/uninstall of a LOADED job that is not wrapped in bin/ade-job-run: allowed ONLY for a KeepAlive service
                        (install: the new definition's KeepAlive; uninstall: the installed plist file's KeepAlive), as a deliberate
                        service restart. The bootout STOPS the running service (not paid-work-safe); the prior bytes and a recovery
                        record are saved first and the prior definition is loaded again if the new one fails. Without the flag
                        such a job is refused (exit 1); with it a canonical-wrapped job takes the normal path; a busy admission lock still refuses
  --allow-no-linger     systemd install/reconcile: proceed when loginctl says Linger=no (default: exit 69 before writing, because
                        user timers stop at logout); never runs sudo, prints `sudo loginctl enable-linger USER`
  --json                list/diff/reconcile: machine-readable output

Auto-detection: darwin with launchctl -> launchd; a booted systemd whose `systemctl --user is-system-running` answers
running/degraded/starting/initializing -> systemd; booted systemd with no reachable user manager -> exit 69 (never a
silent cron); otherwise crontab on PATH -> cron. Placeholders __ADE__ and __HOME__ are always filled; any other
__NAME__ or @NAME@ left unfilled is exit 2, and so is an EnvironmentVariables name that looks like a secret
(KEY/TOKEN/SECRET/PASSWORD). A oneshot systemd job gets KillMode=process (setsid-detached children survive, as on
launchd; plist key KillMode overrides), TimeoutStartSec=max(3 x StartInterval, 300s) and AccuracySec=1s. On systemd and
cron, ~/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin go first in PATH (plist PATHs are Mac paths).

list/diff/reconcile read config/install.toml [install.jobs] / [install.retired_jobs] (S4b) and load the install catalog
only then (so backend/install/status stay usable on Python 3.10 without tomllib). diff never unloads any job,
including foreign owners (Orca/BB/herdr and unknown labels are reported only). reconcile writes ADE-owned
ade-sched jobs on launchd, systemd user units, and user crontab (RECONCILE_WRITE_BACKENDS), creates/deletes
ADE-owned paseo schedules (ledger backend=paseo), removes only labels recorded in the ownership ledger
(~/.local/state/djbclark-ade/jobs.json or ADE_JOBS_STATE_DIR), and never unloads foreign/unknown owners or
root/--system units. A Paseo probe timeout/launch error or a failed host-backend scan is reported as
unknown, never as an empty job list.

Overrides (env): ADE_SCHED_LAUNCHCTL, ADE_SCHED_SYSTEMCTL, ADE_SCHED_LOGINCTL, ADE_SCHED_CRONTAB (binaries);
ADE_SCHED_LAUNCH_AGENTS (default ~/Library/LaunchAgents), ADE_SCHED_UNIT_DIR (default
${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/systemd/user), ADE_SCHED_LOCK (the crontab edit lock, default
${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/ade/ade-sched.lock); ADE_JOBS_STATE_DIR (ownership ledger dir, default
~/.local/state/djbclark-ade).

exit: 6 durable reconcile deferral (admission/drain/migration); 0 ok; 1 an activation command failed (its stderr is quoted) or diff found ADE drift or reconcile had a
blocked/failed step; 2 bad job or usage (also: reconcile --yes on a non-write host backend with no paseo work); 3 status:
a LABEL is not installed; 69 no usable scheduler (none forced, none found, systemd user manager unreachable, Linger=no
on a systemd install without --allow-no-linger, KeepAlive or a StartInterval under 60 s on cron). A `crontab -l`
failure other than "no crontab" is exit 1 and the crontab is left untouched.

Notes and warnings (unmapped plist keys, cron rounding) go to stderr and do not change the exit status.
docs/scheduling.md is the manual.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import json
import os
import sys
from pathlib import Path

sys.path[:0] = [d for d in (os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)),) if d not in sys.path]   # python3 -I has no script dir
import ade_sched

# ade_install (and its tomllib via ade_config) is imported only inside list/diff/reconcile. Other
# subcommands must stay usable on Python 3.10 hosts (Ubuntu 22.04) that lack tomllib.


class _Parser(argparse.ArgumentParser):
    def error(self, message: str) -> None:   # argparse's own exit 2 is our usage code; keep the doc's usage text
        print(__doc__.split("\n\n", 2)[1], file=sys.stderr)
        print(f"ade-sched: {message}", file=sys.stderr)
        raise SystemExit(ade_sched.EX_USAGE)


def _common(p: argparse.ArgumentParser, top: bool) -> None:
    """The options, on the top parser (with the defaults) and on every subcommand (SUPPRESS: set only when given there)."""
    def dflt(v: object) -> dict[str, object]:
        return {"default": v if top else argparse.SUPPRESS}
    p.add_argument("--backend", choices=("auto", *ade_sched.BACKENDS), **dflt("auto"))
    p.add_argument("--ade", metavar="DIR", **dflt(None))
    p.add_argument("--root", metavar="DIR", **dflt(None))
    # its own dest on a subcommand: an append there would REPLACE the top-level list, dropping earlier --set values
    p.add_argument("--set", action="append", metavar="KEY=VALUE", dest="subst" if top else "sub_subst", **dflt([]))
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", dest="dry_run" if top else "sub_dry_run", **dflt(False))
    p.add_argument("--yes", action="store_true", dest="yes" if top else "sub_yes", **dflt(False))
    p.add_argument("--name", action="append", metavar="NAME", dest="names" if top else "sub_names", **dflt([]))
    p.add_argument("--no-activate", action="store_true", **dflt(False))
    p.add_argument("--allow-no-linger", action="store_true", **dflt(False))
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", **dflt(False))


def parse(argv: list[str]) -> argparse.Namespace:
    ap = _Parser(prog="ade-sched", description="install a launchd plist on launchd, systemd or cron",
                 formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter, epilog=__doc__)
    _common(ap, top=True)
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True, parser_class=_Parser)
    for name, arg, nargs in (("backend", None, None), ("render", "plist", None), ("install", "plist", None), ("migrate-wrapper", "plist", None),
                             ("uninstall", "label", None), ("status", "labels", "*"),
                             ("list", None, None), ("diff", None, None), ("reconcile", None, None)):
        sp = sub.add_parser(name)
        _common(sp, top=False)
        if arg:
            sp.add_argument(arg, nargs=nargs) if nargs else sp.add_argument(arg)
        if name in ("install", "uninstall"):
            sp.add_argument("--restart-service", action="store_true")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    a.subst = [*a.subst, *getattr(a, "sub_subst", [])]   # --set before and after the subcommand both count
    a.names = [*a.names, *getattr(a, "sub_names", [])]
    if getattr(a, "sub_dry_run", False):
        a.dry_run = True
    if getattr(a, "sub_yes", False):
        a.yes = True
    return a


def _subst(a: argparse.Namespace) -> dict[str, str]:
    subst: dict[str, str] = {}   # __ADE__/__HOME__ come from Job.from_plist(ade=...), which knows whether --ade was given
    for item in a.subst:
        key, sep, val = item.partition("=")
        if not sep or not key:
            raise ade_sched.SchedError(ade_sched.EX_USAGE, f"--set wants KEY=VALUE, not {item!r}")
        subst[key] = val
    return subst


def _catalog_root(a: argparse.Namespace) -> Path:
    if a.root:
        return Path(a.root)
    if a.ade:
        return Path(a.ade)
    return Path(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))))


def _cmd_list(a: argparse.Namespace) -> int:
    import ade_install as ai  # deferred: tomllib/3.11 only needed for catalog list/diff/reconcile

    try:
        catalog = ai.load_catalog(root=_catalog_root(a))
    except ai.InstallError as e:
        print(f"ade-sched: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return ade_sched.EX_USAGE
    if a.json:
        json.dump(
            {"jobs": catalog.jobs, "retired_jobs": catalog.retired_jobs},
            sys.stdout,
            indent=2,
            sort_keys=True,
        )
        sys.stdout.write("\n")
        return 0
    lines = ade_sched.format_job_list(catalog.jobs, catalog.retired_jobs)
    print(f"ade-sched list: {len(catalog.jobs)} jobs, {len(catalog.retired_jobs)} retired")
    for line in lines:
        print(line)
    return 0


def _cmd_diff(a: argparse.Namespace) -> int:
    import ade_install as ai  # deferred: tomllib/3.11 only needed for catalog list/diff/reconcile

    try:
        catalog = ai.load_catalog(root=_catalog_root(a))
    except ai.InstallError as e:
        print(f"ade-sched: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return ade_sched.EX_USAGE
    backend = None if a.backend == "auto" else a.backend
    live = ade_sched.scan_live(backend)
    rows = ade_sched.diff_jobs(catalog.jobs, catalog.retired_jobs, live, unload=False)
    failed = sum(1 for r in rows if r.fail)
    if a.json:
        json.dump(
            {
                "backend": live.backend,
                "live": [{"id": j.id, "backend": j.backend, "source": j.source, "active": j.active}
                         for j in live.jobs],
                "notes": list(live.notes),
                "drift": [
                    {
                        "name": r.name,
                        "status": r.status,
                        "owner": r.owner,
                        "detail": r.detail,
                        "category": r.category,
                        "fail": r.fail,
                        "action": r.action,
                    }
                    for r in rows
                ],
                "ok": failed == 0,
            },
            sys.stdout,
            indent=2,
            sort_keys=True,
        )
        sys.stdout.write("\n")
    else:
        print(
            f"ade-sched diff: backend={live.backend} live={len(live.jobs)} "
            f"drift_rows={len(rows)} (report only; never unload)"
        )
        for r in rows:
            mark = "FAIL" if r.fail else r.status
            print(f"  {mark:9} {r.category}/{r.name} owner={r.owner}: {r.detail}")
    return 1 if failed else 0


def _cmd_reconcile(a: argparse.Namespace) -> int:
    import ade_install as ai  # deferred: tomllib/3.11 only needed for catalog list/diff/reconcile

    if a.yes and a.dry_run:
        print("ade-sched reconcile: refuse both --yes and --dry-run", file=sys.stderr)
        return ade_sched.EX_USAGE
    dry_run = not a.yes  # default dry-run; --yes executes
    try:
        catalog = ai.load_catalog(root=_catalog_root(a))
    except ai.InstallError as e:
        print(f"ade-sched: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return ade_sched.EX_USAGE
    backend = None if a.backend == "auto" else a.backend
    names = set(a.names) if a.names else None
    results, rc = ade_sched.reconcile(
        catalog.jobs,
        catalog.retired_jobs,
        dry_run=dry_run,
        backend=backend,
        root=_catalog_root(a),
        ade=a.ade,
        names=names,
        allow_no_linger=a.allow_no_linger,
        activate=not a.no_activate,
        extra_subst=_subst(a),
        native_admission=True,
    )
    mode = "dry-run" if dry_run else "yes"
    ledger_path = str(ade_sched.jobs_ledger_path())
    if a.json:
        json.dump(
            {
                "ok": rc == 0,
                "mode": mode,
                "ledger": ledger_path,
                "write_backend": ade_sched.RECONCILE_WRITE_BACKEND,
                "write_backends": sorted(ade_sched.RECONCILE_WRITE_BACKENDS),
                "results": results,
            },
            sys.stdout,
            indent=2,
            sort_keys=True,
        )
        sys.stdout.write("\n")
    else:
        label = "OK" if rc == 0 else "FAIL"
        backends = "/".join(sorted(ade_sched.RECONCILE_WRITE_BACKENDS))
        print(
            f"ade-sched reconcile ({mode}): {label} "
            f"({backends} write path; never unload foreign; ledger={ledger_path})"
        )
        for row in results:
            print(
                f"  {row.get('action', '?'):16} {row.get('category', 'job')}/{row.get('name')} "
                f"owner={row.get('owner')}: {row.get('detail')}"
            )
    return rc


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
    a = parse(sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv)
    if a.ade and not os.path.isdir(a.ade):
        print(f"ade-sched: --ade {a.ade} is not a directory", file=sys.stderr)
        return ade_sched.EX_USAGE
    if a.root and not os.path.isdir(a.root):
        print(f"ade-sched: --root {a.root} is not a directory", file=sys.stderr)
        return ade_sched.EX_USAGE
    backend = None if a.backend == "auto" else a.backend
    try:
        if a.cmd == "list":
            return _cmd_list(a)
        if a.cmd == "diff":
            return _cmd_diff(a)
        if a.cmd == "reconcile":
            return _cmd_reconcile(a)
        if a.cmd == "backend":
            b = ade_sched.detect(backend)
            print(f"backend: {b.name} ({b.reason})")
            if b.name == "launchd":
                print(f"agents: {ade_sched.launch_agents_dir(b.env)}")
            elif b.name == "systemd":
                print(f"units: {ade_sched.unit_dir(b.env)}")
                print(f"linger: {ade_sched.linger(b.env) or 'unknown'}")
            else:
                print(f"crontab: {ade_sched.tool('crontab', b.env)}")
            return 0
        if a.cmd in ("render", "install"):
            job = ade_sched.Job.from_plist(a.plist, _subst(a), ade=a.ade)
            if a.cmd == "render":
                r = ade_sched.render(job, ade_sched.detect(backend))
                for n in r.notes:
                    print(f"ade-sched: note: {n}", file=sys.stderr)
                ade_sched.print_artifacts(r, sys.stdout)
                return 0
            r = ade_sched.install(job, backend, dry_run=a.dry_run, activate=not a.no_activate,
                                  allow_no_linger=a.allow_no_linger, restart_service=a.restart_service)
            if not a.dry_run:
                print(f"ade-sched: installed {job.label} on {r.backend}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 0
        if a.cmd == "migrate-wrapper":
            job = ade_sched.Job.from_plist(a.plist, _subst(a), ade=a.ade)
            r = ade_sched.render(job, ade_sched.detect(backend))
            if r.backend != "launchd":
                raise ade_sched.SchedError(ade_sched.EX_USAGE, "migrate-wrapper is for launchd jobs")
            if a.dry_run:
                print(f"# migrate {job.label}: refuse unless idle, then bootout, write, bootstrap under the canonical lock", file=sys.stderr)
                return 0
            print(f"ade-sched: {ade_sched.migrate_wrapper_launchd(job, next(iter(r.files.values())))} {job.label}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 0
        if a.cmd == "uninstall":
            found = ade_sched.uninstall(a.label, backend, dry_run=a.dry_run, activate=not a.no_activate, ade=a.ade,
                                       restart_service=a.restart_service)
            if not a.dry_run:
                print(f"ade-sched: {'removed' if found else 'not installed:'} {a.label}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 0
        b = ade_sched.detect(backend)
        labels = a.labels or ade_sched.installed_labels(b)
        missing = 0
        for label in labels:
            s = ade_sched.status(label, b)
            missing += not s.installed
            act = "unknown" if s.active is None else "active" if s.active else "inactive"
            print(f"{label}\t{s.backend}\t{'installed' if s.installed else 'not-installed'}\t{act}\t"
                  f"next={s.next_run or '-'}")
        return ade_sched.EX_NOT_INSTALLED if missing and a.labels else 0
    except ade_sched.SchedError as e:
        print(f"ade-sched: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return e.code


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
